   "subject": "Re: [shinyapps-users] Source for Admin Dashboard application usage graph?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Scott,<div><br></div><div>The graphs are drawn using a javascript library called <a href=\"http://www.flotcharts.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.flotcharts.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360928150000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1C-DLPZJLz7n1vc4OKrhXc\">flot</a> which gets it&#39;s data from the <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360928150000&amp;usg=AOvVaw16uOVTme_1PVIqBw_sFiEY\">shinyapps.io</a> API in a custom format. </div><div><br></div><div>That said, if you&#39;re building a shiny dashboard, you might be interested in the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/shinyapps-users/rgug4ftiD2c/YvnSIpKTAQAJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/shinyapps-users/rgug4ftiD2c/YvnSIpKTAQAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360928150000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1H_VzFWCNuwQoTJGWc60A8\">showUsage</a> API that is part of the rsconnect package which will return this same data do you as a data frame. You might also be interested in the <a href=\"https://rstudio.github.io/dygraphs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rstudio.github.io/dygraphs/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360928150000&amp;usg=AOvVaw23vWE7sl2ag1ADnfLncywV\">dygraph package</a> for plotting time series data in shiny applications.</div><div><br></div><div>Hope that helps.</div><div>-Andy</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, May 30, 2017 at 5:25 PM, Scott Goley <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">scott...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
